-- wra1-ch3-general.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), Part 1, Chapter 3 (sections 30 to 43), part wra1.
-- LAYER 1, the law objectively: it takes nobody's point of view.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script, not the official text.
-- A line `-- src:N | text` copies line N of that file (produced by srcrefs.py, never retyped).
--
-- How to read an answer (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed and not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md):
--   JUST FALSE / FALSE  = the text says no in its own words (the quoted words are in a FALSE-kind comment on the branch)
--   NOTHING             = not covered (the reason is in a NOTHING-kind comment on the branch)
-- Sections 30, 31, 34, 35, 36 only point at Schedules; sections 32, 41 (except the two limits) 42 and 43 are
-- regulation-making machinery. They have no function here; NOTES.md gives each its row and its reason.

§ `Section 33 -- Abolition of benefits`

-- src:382 | (1) The following benefits are abolished—
-- src:383 | (a) income-based jobseeker's allowance under the Jobseekers Act 1995;
-- src:384 | (b) income-related employment and support allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007;
-- src:385 | (c) income support under section 124 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992;
-- src:386 | (d) housing benefit under section 130 of that Act;
-- src:387 | (e) council tax benefit under section 131 of that Act;
-- src:388 | (f) child tax credit and working tax credit under the Tax Credits Act 2002.
@ref s 33(1) (src:382-388)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the benefit is abolished` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    -- yes: named in s 33(1)(a)-(f)
    WHEN `income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `income-related employment and support allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `income support` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `housing benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `council tax benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `child tax credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `working tax credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following benefits are abolished" does not say that no other benefit is
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:389 | (2) In subsection (1)—
-- src:390 | (a) “income-based jobseeker's allowance” has the same meaning as in the Jobseekers Act 1995;
@ref s 33(2)(a) (src:389-390)
GIVEN `it has the meaning it has in the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(2)(a) the allowance is income-based jobseeker's allowance` MEANS
    -- the meaning is the Jobseekers Act 1995's, which is not among the sources: the borrowed fact is asked
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the same meaning as in the Jobseekers Act 1995" (a definition by reference)
    `it has the meaning it has in the Jobseekers Act 1995`

-- src:391 | (b) “income-related employment and support allowance” means an employment and support allowance entitlement to which is based on section 1(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007.
@ref s 33(2)(b) (src:391-391)
GIVEN `entitlement to it is based on section 1(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(2)(b) the allowance is income-related employment and support allowance` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an employment and support allowance entitlement to which is based on section 1(2)(b)"
    `entitlement to it is based on section 1(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`

§ `Section 37 -- Capability for work or work-related activity`

-- src:401 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a claimant has limited capability for work if—
-- src:402 | (a) the claimant's capability for work is limited by their physical or mental condition, and
-- src:403 | (b) the limitation is such that it is not reasonable to require the claimant to work.
@ref s 37(1) (src:401-403)
GIVEN `the capability for work is limited by the physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitation makes it unreasonable to require the claimant to work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(1) the claimant has limited capability for work on the Act's own test` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has limited capability for work if (a) ... and (b) ..." (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a))
    `the capability for work is limited by the physical or mental condition`
    AND `the limitation makes it unreasonable to require the claimant to work`

-- src:404 | (2) For the purposes of this Part a claimant has limited capability for work-related activity if—
-- src:405 | (a) the claimant's capability for work-related activity is limited by their physical or mental condition, and
-- src:406 | (b) the limitation is such that it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake work-related activity.
@ref s 37(2) (src:404-406)
GIVEN `the capability for work-related activity is limited by the physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limitation makes it unreasonable to require the claimant to undertake work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 37(2) the claimant has limited capability for work-related activity on the Act's own test` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has limited capability for work-related activity if (a) ... and (b) ..." (a failed "if": lawyer's reading (a))
    `the capability for work-related activity is limited by the physical or mental condition`
    AND `the limitation makes it unreasonable to require the claimant to undertake work-related activity`

-- s 37(3): the question is determined in accordance with regulations; the regulations are not among the sources, so the
-- caller supplies the determination (for example the outcome of an assessment under s 37(4)). Subsections (4) to (9) are
-- regulation-making powers about how the assessment is done.
-- src:407 | (3) The question whether a claimant has limited capability for work or work-related activity for the purposes of this Part is to be determined in accordance with regulations.
@ref s 37(3) (src:407-407)
GIVEN `the determination made in accordance with regulations under section 37` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(3) the claimant has limited capability as determined in accordance with regulations` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the determination made in accordance with regulations under section 37`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (a supplied regulation says no): the supplied determination is "no" ("is to be determined in accordance with regulations")
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 38 -- Information`

-- src:419 | Information supplied under Chapter 2 of this Part or section 37 is to be taken for all purposes to be information relating to social security.
@ref s 38 (src:419-419)
GIVEN `it was supplied under Chapter 2 of this Part or section 37` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38 the information is information relating to social security` MEANS
    IF `it was supplied under Chapter 2 of this Part or section 37`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section says nothing about information supplied in any other way
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 39 -- Couples`

-- src:421 | (1) In this Part “couple” means—
-- src:422 | (a) two people who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are members of the same household; or
-- src:423 | (b) two people who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@ref s 39(1) (src:421-423)
GIVEN `the two people` IS A `Two people`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) the two people are a couple` MEANS
    `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part 'couple' means" limbs (a) and (b); neither limb is a couple
    WHERE
        -- limb (a): married or civil partners, and members of the same household
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            `the two people`'s `their relationship`'s `married to each other or civil partners of each other`
            AND `the two people`'s `their relationship`'s `members of the same household`
        -- limb (b): not married or civil partners, but living together as if they were
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            (NOT `the two people`'s `their relationship`'s `married to each other or civil partners of each other`)
            AND `the two people`'s `their relationship`'s `living together as if married or civil partners`

-- s 39(3): regulations may prescribe circumstances (a) in which a marriage or civil partnership is disregarded,
-- (b) in which two people are treated as living together as if married, (c) in which people are treated as being or not
-- being members of the same household. The regulations are not among the sources, so each is an input; NOTHING means "no
-- such regulations supplied", and then the Act's own words (s 39(1)) apply.
-- src:425 | (3) For the purposes of this section regulations may prescribe—
-- src:426 | (a) circumstances in which the fact that two persons are married or are civil partners is to be disregarded;
-- src:427 | (b) circumstances in which two people are to be treated as living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners;
-- src:428 | (c) circumstances in which people are to be treated as being or not being members of the same household.
@ref s 39(3) (src:425-428)
GIVEN `the two people` IS A `Two people`
      `regulations disregard the marriage or civil partnership` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the two as living together as if married or civil partners` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `regulations treat the two as members of the same household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(3) the two people are a couple once the regulations supplied are applied` MEANS
    `limb (a) as treated` OR `limb (b) as treated`
    WHERE
        `limb (a) as treated` MEANS `married as treated` AND `household as treated`
        `limb (b) as treated` MEANS (NOT `married as treated`) AND `living together as treated`
        `married as treated` MEANS
            CONSIDER `regulations disregard the marriage or civil partnership`
            -- FALSE-kind (a supplied regulation says no): regulations disregard the marriage or civil partnership (s 39(3)(a))
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE `the two people`'s `their relationship`'s `married to each other or civil partners of each other`
        `household as treated` MEANS
            CONSIDER `regulations treat the two as members of the same household`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (a supplied regulation says no): regulations treat the two as not being members of the same household (s 39(3)(c))
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN FALSE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the two people`'s `their relationship`'s `members of the same household`
        `living together as treated` MEANS
            CONSIDER `regulations treat the two as living together as if married or civil partners`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE `the two people`'s `their relationship`'s `living together as if married or civil partners`

§ `Section 40 -- Interpretation of Part 1`

-- The terms s 40 defines or points to. One constructor for each entry of the list (raw lines 431 to 454); "limited
-- capability for work" and "limited capability for work-related activity" are one entry (line 438) with two terms.
DECLARE `s 40 defined term` IS ONE OF
    `s 40 assessment period`
    `s 40 child`
    `s 40 claim`
    `s 40 claimant`
    `s 40 couple`
    `s 40 disabled`
    `s 40 joint claimants`
    `s 40 limited capability for work`
    `s 40 limited capability for work-related activity`
    `s 40 prescribed`
    `s 40 primary legislation`
    `s 40 qualifying young person`
    `s 40 regular and substantial caring responsibilities`
    `s 40 responsible carer`
    `s 40 secondary legislation`
    `s 40 severely disabled`
    `s 40 single claimant`
    `s 40 single person`
    `s 40 work`
    `s 40 work availability requirement`
    `s 40 work preparation requirement`
    `s 40 work search requirement`
    `s 40 work-focused interview requirement`
    `s 40 work-related activity`
    `s 40 work-related requirement`

-- Where each term gets its meaning: the provision of this Act it points to, "section 40" where s 40 itself says what the
-- term means, or "regulations" where the term "has such meaning as may be prescribed".
-- src:430 | In this Part—
-- src:431 | “assessment period” has the meaning given by section 7(2);
-- src:432 | “child” means a person under the age of 16;
-- src:433 | “claim” means claim for universal credit;
-- src:434 | “claimant” means a single claimant or each of joint claimants;
-- src:435 | “couple” has the meaning given by section 39;
-- src:436 | “disabled” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:437 | “joint claimants” means members of a couple who jointly make a claim or in relation to whom an award of universal credit is made;
-- src:438 | “limited capability for work” and “limited capability for work-related activity” are to be construed in accordance with section 37(1) and (2);
-- src:439 | “prescribed” means specified or provided for in regulations;
-- src:440 | “primary legislation” means an Act, Act of the Scottish Parliament or Act or Measure of the National Assembly for Wales;
-- src:441 | “qualifying young person” has the meaning given in section 10(5);
-- src:442 | “regular and substantial caring responsibilities” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:443 | “responsible carer”, in relation to a child, has the meaning given in section 19(6);
-- src:444 | “secondary legislation” means an instrument made under primary legislation”;
-- src:445 | “severely disabled” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:446 | “single claimant” means a single person who makes a claim for universal credit or in relation to whom an award of universal credit is made as a single person;
-- src:447 | “single person” is to be construed in accordance with section 1(2)(a);
-- src:448 | “work” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:449 | “work availability requirement” has the meaning given by section 18(1);
-- src:450 | “work preparation requirement” has the meaning given by section 16(1);
-- src:451 | “work search requirement” has the meaning given by section 17(1);
-- src:452 | “work-focused interview requirement” has the meaning given by section 15(1);
-- src:453 | “work-related activity”, in relation to a person, means activity which makes it more likely that the person will obtain or remain in work or be able to do so;
-- src:454 | “work-related requirement” has the meaning given by section 13(2).
@ref s 40 (the list) (src:430-454)
GIVEN term IS A `s 40 defined term`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 40 where the meaning is given` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `s 40 assessment period` THEN "section 7(2)"
    WHEN `s 40 child` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 claim` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 claimant` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 couple` THEN "section 39"
    WHEN `s 40 disabled` THEN "regulations"
    WHEN `s 40 joint claimants` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 limited capability for work` THEN "section 37(1)"
    WHEN `s 40 limited capability for work-related activity` THEN "section 37(2)"
    WHEN `s 40 prescribed` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 primary legislation` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 qualifying young person` THEN "section 10(5)"
    WHEN `s 40 regular and substantial caring responsibilities` THEN "regulations"
    WHEN `s 40 responsible carer` THEN "section 19(6)"
    WHEN `s 40 secondary legislation` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 severely disabled` THEN "regulations"
    WHEN `s 40 single claimant` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 single person` THEN "section 1(2)(a)"
    WHEN `s 40 work` THEN "regulations"
    WHEN `s 40 work availability requirement` THEN "section 18(1)"
    WHEN `s 40 work preparation requirement` THEN "section 16(1)"
    WHEN `s 40 work search requirement` THEN "section 17(1)"
    WHEN `s 40 work-focused interview requirement` THEN "section 15(1)"
    WHEN `s 40 work-related activity` THEN "section 40"
    WHEN `s 40 work-related requirement` THEN "section 13(2)"

-- "child" means a person under the age of 16. `age in years` is completed years (wra-core), so "under 16" is "less than 16".
-- src:432 | “child” means a person under the age of 16;
@ref s 40 "child" (src:432-432)
GIVEN person IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the person is a child` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'child' means a person under the age of 16"
    person's `age in years` LESS THAN 16

-- src:433 | “claim” means claim for universal credit;
@ref s 40 "claim" (src:433-433)
GIVEN `it is a claim for universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the claim is a claim in this Part` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'claim' means claim for universal credit"
    `it is a claim for universal credit`

-- "claimant" means a single claimant or each of joint claimants: the people the claim is about.
-- src:434 | “claimant” means a single claimant or each of joint claimants;
@ref s 40 "claimant" (src:434-434)
GIVEN claimants IS A Claimants
GIVETH A LIST OF Person
`s 40 the claimants` MEANS
    CONSIDER claimants
    WHEN `a single claimant` person THEN LIST person
    WHEN `joint claimants` two THEN LIST two's `the first person`, two's `the second person`

-- "joint claimants" means members of a couple who jointly make a claim or in relation to whom an award of universal credit is made.
-- src:437 | “joint claimants” means members of a couple who jointly make a claim or in relation to whom an award of universal credit is made;
@ref s 40 "joint claimants" (src:437-437)
GIVEN `the two people` IS A `Two people`
      `they jointly make a claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an award of universal credit is made in relation to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the two people are joint claimants` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'joint claimants' means members of a couple who jointly make a claim or ..."
    `s 39(1) the two people are a couple` `the two people`
    AND (`they jointly make a claim` OR `an award of universal credit is made in relation to them`)

-- "single claimant" means a single person who makes a claim for universal credit or in relation to whom an award of
-- universal credit is made as a single person.
-- src:446 | “single claimant” means a single person who makes a claim for universal credit or in relation to whom an award of universal credit is made as a single person;
@ref s 40 "single claimant" (src:446-446)
GIVEN `the person is a single person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes a claim for universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an award is made in relation to the person as a single person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the person is a single claimant` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'single claimant' means a single person who makes a claim for universal credit or ..."
    `the person is a single person`
    AND (`the person makes a claim for universal credit` OR `an award is made in relation to the person as a single person`)

-- src:439 | “prescribed” means specified or provided for in regulations;
@ref s 40 "prescribed" (src:439-439)
GIVEN `it is specified or provided for in regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'prescribed' means specified or provided for in regulations"
    `it is specified or provided for in regulations`

DECLARE `s 40 kind of legislation` IS ONE OF
    `s 40 an Act`
    `s 40 an Act of the Scottish Parliament`
    `s 40 an Act of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `s 40 a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales`
    `s 40 an instrument made under primary legislation`
    `s 40 some other kind of legislation`

-- src:440 | “primary legislation” means an Act, Act of the Scottish Parliament or Act or Measure of the National Assembly for Wales;
@ref s 40 "primary legislation" (src:440-440)
GIVEN legislation IS A `s 40 kind of legislation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the legislation is primary legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER legislation
    WHEN `s 40 an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 40 an Act of the Scottish Parliament` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 40 an Act of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 40 a Measure of the National Assembly for Wales` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'primary legislation' means an Act, Act of the Scottish Parliament or Act or Measure of the National Assembly for Wales"
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The stray closing quote at the end of the raw line (`”;`) is printed in the quotation as it is in the text (PLAN.md section 5, item 7).
-- src:444 | “secondary legislation” means an instrument made under primary legislation”;
@ref s 40 "secondary legislation" (src:444-444)
GIVEN `it is an instrument made under primary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the instrument is secondary legislation` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'secondary legislation' means an instrument made under primary legislation"
    `it is an instrument made under primary legislation`

-- src:453 | “work-related activity”, in relation to a person, means activity which makes it more likely that the person will obtain or remain in work or be able to do so;
@ref s 40 "work-related activity" (src:453-453)
GIVEN `it is activity which makes it more likely that the person will obtain or remain in work or be able to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 40 the activity is work-related activity` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'work-related activity' ... means activity which makes it more likely that the person will obtain or remain in work or be able to do so"
    `it is activity which makes it more likely that the person will obtain or remain in work or be able to do so`

-- "disabled", "regular and substantial caring responsibilities", "severely disabled" and "work" each "has such meaning as
-- may be prescribed" (raw lines 436, 442, 445, 448). The regulations are not among the sources, so the caller supplies
-- the answer the regulations give for the person or matter; for any other term this function has no answer.
-- src:436 | “disabled” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:437 | “joint claimants” means members of a couple who jointly make a claim or in relation to whom an award of universal credit is made;
-- src:438 | “limited capability for work” and “limited capability for work-related activity” are to be construed in accordance with section 37(1) and (2);
-- src:439 | “prescribed” means specified or provided for in regulations;
-- src:440 | “primary legislation” means an Act, Act of the Scottish Parliament or Act or Measure of the National Assembly for Wales;
-- src:441 | “qualifying young person” has the meaning given in section 10(5);
-- src:442 | “regular and substantial caring responsibilities” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:443 | “responsible carer”, in relation to a child, has the meaning given in section 19(6);
-- src:444 | “secondary legislation” means an instrument made under primary legislation”;
-- src:445 | “severely disabled” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
-- src:446 | “single claimant” means a single person who makes a claim for universal credit or in relation to whom an award of universal credit is made as a single person;
-- src:447 | “single person” is to be construed in accordance with section 1(2)(a);
-- src:448 | “work” has such meaning as may be prescribed;
@ref s 40 (the terms that have a prescribed meaning) (src:436-448)
GIVEN term IS A `s 40 defined term`
      `the answer the regulations give` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 40 the person or matter has the prescribed meaning of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `s 40 disabled` THEN `the answer the regulations give`
    WHEN `s 40 regular and substantial caring responsibilities` THEN `the answer the regulations give`
    WHEN `s 40 severely disabled` THEN `the answer the regulations give`
    WHEN `s 40 work` THEN `the answer the regulations give`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the supplied answer is NOTHING the regulations are not among the sources
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): any other term has its meaning from the Act (see `s 40 where the meaning is given`), not from regulations
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 41 -- Pilot schemes (the two limits the section states)`

-- A pilot scheme "may not have effect for a period exceeding three years" (36 months).
-- src:475 | (5) A pilot scheme may not have effect for a period exceeding three years, but—
-- src:476 | (a) the Secretary of State may by order made by statutory instrument provide that the pilot scheme is to continue to have effect after the time when it would otherwise expire for a period not exceeding twelve months (and may make more than one such order);
-- src:477 | (b) a pilot scheme may be replaced by a further pilot scheme making the same or similar provision.
@ref s 41(5) (src:475-477)
GIVEN `the months the pilot scheme has effect for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(5) the pilot scheme's own period is within three years` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A pilot scheme may not have effect for a period exceeding three years"
    `the months the pilot scheme has effect for` AT MOST 36

-- The Secretary of State may continue a pilot scheme by order "for a period not exceeding twelve months".
@ref s 41(5)(a) (src:476-476)
GIVEN `the months the order continues the pilot scheme for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(5)(a) the order's continuation is within twelve months` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding twelve months"
    `the months the order continues the pilot scheme for` AT MOST 12
